2.3.evidence:
CHAPTER VI
ROLE OF GOVERNMENT, PRIVATE SECTOR AND COMMUNITY INSTITUTIONS Article 11 (1) To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall conduct empowerment and awareness raising to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows: a. Increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. Providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. Providing employment opportunities for women;
d. Building community participation and concern towards prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. Building and providing an information system that is easily accessible; f. Building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children;
g. Optimizing integrated service centers for women and child empowerment (P2TP2A) or other designations as protection posts for women and children from acts of violence; and
h. Opening community-based complaint posts for the protection of women and children.

3.5.evidence:
CHAPTER VII
SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 13
(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence are as follows:
a. Complaint services;
b. Health services;
c. Legal services;
d. Repatriation;
e. Recovery, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. Identification services;
g. Psychological services; and
